      "message": "With this use case, the similarities with ClearBufferInfo and compute being able to take better advantage of knowing the binding size as well, I think we will want to consolidate all of these structs into `BindBufferInfo` and just store `fOffset` and `fSize` as `uint32_t`\u0027s to keep the size the same as before. \n\nI do not think we need 64-bits to represent a GPU buffer size or offset with the other content restrictions Graphite imposes.\n\nI\u0027m fine leaving this in for now, however, because I think it\u0027s a bit more work to keep the `fSize` valid for the dynamic vertex buffers that just discard that info right now. I created a bug to do this clean up, if you can add a `TODO(b/308933713): Add size to BindBufferInfo instead`?",
